Subject: Cantor Semantic Inspection Stdio Host P0 Plan

@ [plan_uuid] eb2c7b5a-954b-44f1-beb4-bd676ea33fee
@ [specification_uuid] 4ee53d21-ed53-4f35-bbaf-06cab3a34085

& [Phase1_PreDispatch]
  + add the exact binary target and isolate argument plus bounded EOF admission from semantic dispatch
  + expose a testable pure disposition core for argument input and publication state where practical

& [Phase2_WireExecution]
  + call respond once only after complete admission
  + preserve returned response bytes without translation and classify all earlier faults into one public host fault

& [Phase3_Publication]
  + write_all and flush exact stdout bytes then return success
  + after output begins suppress alternate stderr and return only nonzero exit on incomplete publication

& [Phase4_Adversarial]
  + test zero arguments exact success nested refusal empty malformed unknown duplicate trailing oversized and raw-bound cases
  + test non-echoing fault output effect counts response equality and static absence

& [Phase5_Closure]
  + run focused dual-profile exact workspace Clippy format dual-host evidence recursive attribution completion signature publication and immediate bookend gates

& [StopConditions]
  + stop on any need for paths filesystem sockets service lifecycle environment provider model shell remote operation or authority widening
  + stop rather than weaken input output fault or exit semantics
